# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify.
#
# The client routes on real paths (/login, /explore, /<projectId>) read from
# window.location.pathname, so a static host that looks for a file at that
# path 404s on every direct link, refresh and shared project URL -- only "/"
# would load.
#
# Note this rule is NOT valid on Cloudflare Workers static assets, which
# applies a stricter validator and rejects it as an infinite loop because
# /index.html matches /* again. Workers uses not_found_handling in
# wrangler.jsonc instead. Pages and Netlify both accept this form.
/*    /index.html   200
